course: dictionary
lesson: 14538
title: Personalised
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Personalised means made specially for one person. Often it has their name or initials on it. «Mia's new bike has a personalised bell with her name on it.» Only Mia's bell has her name, so it was made just for her.
explain: Personalised can also mean changed to suit one person's needs or likes. «The teacher made a personalised reading plan for each child.» Each plan fits that child's reading level and interests, not everyone's.
explain: To personalise something is to make it your own. «Ben personalised his water bottle with stickers of his favourite football team.» Ben changed the bottle so it shows who it belongs to.
fact: Personalised means made specially for one person.
fact: «Personalised» can describe a gift, a plan, a bag or a number plate.
fact: «Personalise» is the verb: to personalise something is to make it your own or suited to you.
fact: Online, personalised adverts and feeds are chosen for you using information about what you click, watch or search.
fact: That is why websites collect data: the data helps them decide what to show you.
exercise: «The shop made a personalised mug with Ruby's name on it.» What does personalised mean here? | Cheap and broken | Very hot | *Made specially for one person | Sold in every shop in the country
exercise: Tom says his app shows him personalised adverts. What does that suggest? | Adverts that never appear | Adverts that are the same for everyone | *Adverts chosen for him from what he has clicked | Adverts that are printed in books
exercise: To personalise something means to | *Make it your own or suited to you | Hide it from your friends | Throw it away | Copy it exactly so it matches everyone else's
test: «Her teacher gave her a personalised spelling list based on the words she gets wrong.» What does personalised mean here? | Meant for everyone in the class | Written in very small writing | Too hard to read | *Chosen to suit Her needs
test: Sam wants to personalise his bedroom door. What is he going to do? | Take it off its hinges | Leave it plain and empty | *Make it his own, for example with his name and pictures | Paint it the same colour as everyone else's
exam: «Dad bought a personalised number plate with our initials on it.» Which word tells you the number plate was made just for our family? | bought | plate | *personalised | number
